1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:06,861
Yes?

2
00:00:07,862 --> 00:00:09,030
-We came.
-We came.

3
00:00:09,114 --> 00:00:10,406
What?!

4
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:12,992
<i>All of us are unemployed,</i>

5
00:00:13,076 --> 00:00:15,912
<i>and on a vacation from life, right?</i>

6
00:00:15,995 --> 00:00:16,996
<i>This way.</i>

7
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:18,790
<i>What? Someone else is here too?</i>

8
00:00:18,873 --> 00:00:20,416
<i>This is my friend, Tetsuro.</i>

9
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,710
<i>A barbecue needs a man's strength!</i>

10
00:00:22,794 --> 00:00:24,003
Who is this handsome guy?

11
00:00:24,087 --> 00:00:26,798
This is Mr. Nishigami,
who takes care of the villas around here.

12
00:00:26,881 --> 00:00:28,299
Mr. Nishigami!

13
00:00:28,383 --> 00:00:29,968
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

14
00:00:30,051 --> 00:00:32,929
<i>At the end of summer,</i>
<i>this villa ground will be hit</i>

15
00:00:33,012 --> 00:00:35,306
<i>by a large-scale landslide</i>
<i>disaster due to a typhoon.</i>

16
00:00:35,390 --> 00:00:37,350
<i>Make sure to report the precise increase</i>

17
00:00:37,433 --> 00:00:39,644
<i>or decrease in the number</i>
<i>of casualties when that happens.</i>

18
00:00:40,145 --> 00:00:42,605
Is it true that you have a villa
in Tatsumi Town?

19
00:00:43,439 --> 00:00:44,607
Mr. Jin?

20
00:00:44,691 --> 00:00:48,027
Can I go there too?

21
00:01:09,465 --> 00:01:11,092
Mr. Jin, get in!

22
00:01:13,678 --> 00:01:14,596
Open it!

23
00:01:14,679 --> 00:01:16,472
Mr. Ichijo!

24
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:22,228
Mr. Ichijo! Please give us a comment!

25
00:01:22,312 --> 00:01:24,731
Please tell us about the situation!

26
00:01:27,901 --> 00:01:29,277
Damn, he got away!

27
00:01:29,944 --> 00:01:31,029
Hello?

28
00:01:31,112 --> 00:01:32,864
Is this the <i>Weekly Shuubun</i>?

29
00:01:55,887 --> 00:01:56,888
Hello.

30
00:01:57,472 --> 00:01:59,307
Oh, hello.

31
00:01:59,974 --> 00:02:02,852
I'm collecting firewood.

32
00:02:03,686 --> 00:02:06,231
You're here on vacation, aren't you?

33
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:08,816
Oh, yes, hello.

34
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,443
Then how about…

35
00:02:11,736 --> 00:02:13,446
doing some fishing?

36
00:02:14,697 --> 00:02:15,865
Fishing?

37
00:02:27,835 --> 00:02:29,045
This is amazing.

38
00:02:29,128 --> 00:02:30,588
It's cold!

39
00:02:31,631 --> 00:02:34,425
We don't have anything
like this in Tokyo. Incredible.

40
00:02:40,306 --> 00:02:42,308
I wonder if I'll catch anything.

41
00:02:42,392 --> 00:02:44,352
I would love to surprise Konta.

42
00:02:48,231 --> 00:02:50,316
I got something! It's biting!

43
00:02:50,984 --> 00:02:51,859
Whoa!

44
00:02:52,735 --> 00:02:53,903
Oh, wow!

45
00:02:55,113 --> 00:02:56,239
Awesome!

46
00:02:57,323 --> 00:02:59,659
I caught one! It's a feisty one!

47
00:02:59,742 --> 00:03:00,952
Just like Konta.

48
00:03:01,744 --> 00:03:03,579
What do I do now…

49
00:03:13,339 --> 00:03:14,173
Fish.

50
00:03:16,843 --> 00:03:19,595
There's a spot nearby
where you can fish for rainbow trout,

51
00:03:19,679 --> 00:03:20,555
so I checked it out.

52
00:03:21,973 --> 00:03:23,933
Oh, fishing…

53
00:03:26,269 --> 00:03:28,229
Are you going to eat those?

54
00:03:28,312 --> 00:03:29,355
Oh, yes.

55
00:03:29,897 --> 00:03:32,567
I'm going to grill them with salt.

56
00:03:34,068 --> 00:03:37,697
So you're having another barbecue today?

57
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:38,906
Yes.

58
00:03:43,369 --> 00:03:45,830
I am so incredibly bored.

59
00:03:45,913 --> 00:03:46,998
Hey!

60
00:03:47,081 --> 00:03:49,208
-Let's watch this show together.
-What?

61
00:03:49,292 --> 00:03:51,753
It's from a little while ago,
but they say it's really good.

62
00:03:51,836 --> 00:03:52,962
What?

63
00:03:54,589 --> 00:03:57,717
I love the whole "he's-a-terrorist
but-he's-also-a-detective" thing.

64
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,552
Oh, I've seen this actor before.

65
00:03:59,635 --> 00:04:00,511
Hey.

66
00:04:00,595 --> 00:04:02,972
If you two are so bored, help me clean up.

67
00:04:03,598 --> 00:04:06,184
Can't, we're watching a show.

68
00:04:06,768 --> 00:04:07,852
Come on!

69
00:04:10,730 --> 00:04:12,648
I'm back.

70
00:04:12,732 --> 00:04:13,858
Welcome back.

71
00:04:13,941 --> 00:04:15,651
Oh, Mr. Nishigami.

72
00:04:15,735 --> 00:04:18,071
I brought some firewood.

73
00:04:18,154 --> 00:04:19,030
Wait, firewood?

74
00:04:19,113 --> 00:04:20,573
Are we doing another barbecue today?

75
00:04:20,656 --> 00:04:22,617
That's great!

76
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:24,952
What's in there?

77
00:04:27,997 --> 00:04:30,958
Today's feast.

78
00:04:32,585 --> 00:04:34,962
They're so pretty! Look how they sparkle!

79
00:04:36,923 --> 00:04:37,799
What?

80
00:04:38,383 --> 00:04:39,384
Welcome back.

81
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:40,468
We're home.

82
00:04:40,551 --> 00:04:42,011
What? Who's this?

83
00:04:42,095 --> 00:04:43,805
Who is this old guy?

84
00:04:44,514 --> 00:04:45,973
What? No way!

85
00:04:46,057 --> 00:04:48,559
It's <i>Terrorist Detective!</i>
It's the guy from <i>Terrorist Detective!</i>

86
00:04:48,643 --> 00:04:49,894
<i>Terrorist Detective</i>, like the…

87
00:04:49,977 --> 00:04:52,188
He's the guy from the show
we were just watching!

88
00:04:52,271 --> 00:04:53,314
Hello.

89
00:04:53,898 --> 00:04:55,358
Wow, it's really him!

90
00:04:55,441 --> 00:04:57,652
Why, how did you end up here, Mr. Jin?

91
00:04:58,694 --> 00:05:00,196
Thanks for your support.

92
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:03,574
I'm the actor, Jin Ichijo.

93
00:05:06,369 --> 00:05:07,412
Yo!

94
00:05:38,025 --> 00:05:40,069
Mr. Jin, come on in!

95
00:05:40,153 --> 00:05:42,321
-Midori, tea! Get some tea!
-Oh, right!

96
00:05:42,405 --> 00:05:44,574
Mr. Jin, I'll take your bag.

97
00:05:44,657 --> 00:05:45,575
Hey.

98
00:05:46,242 --> 00:05:47,910
Is it really okay for an old guy like me

99
00:05:47,994 --> 00:05:50,955
to crash with a bunch
of young kids like this?

100
00:05:51,038 --> 00:05:52,874
What are they, students?

101
00:05:52,957 --> 00:05:55,168
No, they're all working adults. Grown-ups!

102
00:05:55,918 --> 00:05:58,421
What about work?
Do they have the day off today?

103
00:05:58,504 --> 00:06:02,008
They're all on an extended le--
Extended brea-- A vacation!

104
00:06:02,091 --> 00:06:03,551
-Take a seat.
-Go ahead.

105
00:06:03,634 --> 00:06:05,178
Hey, why?

106
00:06:05,261 --> 00:06:07,555
Why is a celebrity
coming to a place like this?

107
00:06:07,638 --> 00:06:09,849
Who is that guy again?

108
00:06:09,932 --> 00:06:12,685
It's Jin Ichijo! From <i>Terrorist Detective!</i>

109
00:06:13,978 --> 00:06:16,856
Hey, AI, tell me about Jin Ichijo.

110
00:06:17,356 --> 00:06:20,693
<i>Jin Ichijo is a veteran Japanese actor</i>

111
00:06:20,776 --> 00:06:24,822
<i>known for his compelling</i>
<i>performances and wide range of roles.</i>

112
00:06:24,906 --> 00:06:26,157
We can hear everything, you know!

113
00:06:27,408 --> 00:06:29,952
<i>His notable works include</i>
Terrorist Detective,

114
00:06:30,036 --> 00:06:33,789
Love's End City,<i> and</i>
From a Western Town in a Northern Country.

115
00:06:33,873 --> 00:06:34,832
Right!

116
00:06:34,916 --> 00:06:38,711
I used to watch
<i>Love's End City </i>when I was a kid!

117
00:06:38,794 --> 00:06:40,046
Oh, he's that guy!

118
00:06:40,129 --> 00:06:42,381
The one who played
the main character's boyfriend!

119
00:06:42,465 --> 00:06:43,466
I'm sorry.

120
00:06:44,592 --> 00:06:47,386
Sorry to keep you waiting, Mr. Jin.

121
00:06:48,179 --> 00:06:50,556
Here's some tea.

122
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:52,099
Oh, really?

123
00:06:52,183 --> 00:06:54,060
You watched that?

124
00:06:54,143 --> 00:06:55,645
I watched it with her, too.

125
00:06:56,187 --> 00:06:58,272
This is my younger sister, Midori.

126
00:06:58,856 --> 00:07:00,107
I see.

127
00:07:00,191 --> 00:07:01,651
What a cute little sister.

128
00:07:01,734 --> 00:07:02,652
Mr. Jin!

129
00:07:02,735 --> 00:07:07,073
Look, I was just watching
<i>Terrorist Detective </i>a second ago!

130
00:07:07,156 --> 00:07:09,325
Why are you watching stuff like that?

131
00:07:12,078 --> 00:07:13,287
Well…

132
00:07:15,665 --> 00:07:17,416
Allow me to introduce myself properly.

133
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,460
I'm Jin Ichijo.

134
00:07:20,753 --> 00:07:24,840
I apologize for dropping in
so suddenly today.

135
00:07:25,633 --> 00:07:31,055
Thanks to my younger colleague, Konta,
I'll be staying here for a little while.

136
00:07:31,138 --> 00:07:32,765
Nice to meet you all.

137
00:07:33,516 --> 00:07:34,392
Amazing!

138
00:07:34,475 --> 00:07:36,894
He looks picture-perfect
just standing there.

139
00:07:36,978 --> 00:07:38,896
He looks way older than he does on TV.

140
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:40,815
Hey, watch your mouth.

141
00:07:40,898 --> 00:07:42,233
Don't worry.

142
00:07:42,316 --> 00:07:43,609
It's fine.

143
00:07:44,485 --> 00:07:46,112
She's right.

144
00:07:47,029 --> 00:07:50,950
An old guy like me
is just getting in the way

145
00:07:51,033 --> 00:07:53,869
of you young people having a good time.

146
00:07:53,953 --> 00:07:55,997
You're not in the way at all!

147
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:59,500
Oh! I want to watch
<i>Terrorist Detective </i>with the actual star

148
00:07:59,584 --> 00:08:01,752
and hear some behind-the-scenes gossip!

149
00:08:01,836 --> 00:08:03,504
Hey, you're being way too pushy!

150
00:08:03,588 --> 00:08:04,714
That's rude.

151
00:08:04,797 --> 00:08:07,049
-You're the rude one, Tsumugi.
-It's fine.

152
00:08:07,592 --> 00:08:09,010
You don't have to be polite with me.

153
00:08:09,594 --> 00:08:11,137
Mind if I watch the Koshien?

154
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:12,471
Wait, don't turn on the TV!

155
00:08:12,555 --> 00:08:13,639
What?

156
00:08:14,557 --> 00:08:18,060
<i>The famous actor, Jin Ichijo, is involved</i>
<i>in a massive cheating scandal.</i>

157
00:08:18,144 --> 00:08:20,062
<i>Yesterday's issue of the </i>Weekly Shuubun

158
00:08:20,146 --> 00:08:23,774
<i>published a scoop featuring photos of him</i>
<i>on dates with three beautiful women,</i>

159
00:08:23,858 --> 00:08:25,818
<i>causing a massive public uproar.</i>

160
00:08:25,901 --> 00:08:27,236
<i>Mr. Jin really did it this time.</i>

161
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:31,282
<i>A blonde </i>gyaru<i>, a model-esque beauty,</i>
<i>and on top of that, one with a black bob.</i>

162
00:08:31,365 --> 00:08:33,075
<i>Aren't they a bit too young?</i>

163
00:08:33,159 --> 00:08:34,577
<i>He's a married man, right?</i>

164
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:37,413
<i>It's pretty shocking</i>
<i>for an actor of his caliber</i>

165
00:08:37,496 --> 00:08:39,498
<i>to be caught in multiple affairs.</i>

166
00:08:43,502 --> 00:08:47,214
It looks like I'm going to have

167
00:08:48,132 --> 00:08:50,134
a much longer break than you all.

168
00:08:50,217 --> 00:08:52,720
Mr. Jin, don't say that, come on!
You're going to be fine!

169
00:08:52,803 --> 00:08:54,513
Mr. Jin, you'll be fine!

170
00:09:01,479 --> 00:09:03,648
You've gotten good at starting fires.

171
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:06,651
Thanks to your guidance.

172
00:09:08,819 --> 00:09:11,781
By the way, are you from overseas?

173
00:09:11,864 --> 00:09:14,200
The way you talk is just kind of…

174
00:09:15,576 --> 00:09:18,204
Oh, but, if you're from overseas,

175
00:09:18,287 --> 00:09:20,665
it would be strange
to have the last name Nishigami.

176
00:09:20,748 --> 00:09:21,999
Right!

177
00:09:22,083 --> 00:09:25,086
Are you Japanese raised abroad?

178
00:09:27,463 --> 00:09:28,798
I've been…

179
00:09:30,466 --> 00:09:32,051
in this town my whole life.

180
00:09:44,563 --> 00:09:48,776
Hey, how do you even know
that guy in the first place?

181
00:09:48,859 --> 00:09:50,820
Did you tell him to run away
and hide out here

182
00:09:50,903 --> 00:09:53,030
after his affair got exposed
and turned into a scandal?

183
00:09:53,114 --> 00:09:56,701
Mr. Jin took really good care of me
when we worked together.

184
00:09:56,784 --> 00:09:57,743
You worked together?

185
00:09:57,827 --> 00:09:59,286
That's amazing! What role did you play?

186
00:09:59,370 --> 00:10:02,832
Mr. Jin was Nobunaga,
and I was Foot Soldier F.

187
00:10:02,915 --> 00:10:03,791
So you were an extra.

188
00:10:04,875 --> 00:10:07,753
He even took me out for food
after shooting wrapped up.

189
00:10:07,837 --> 00:10:10,464
He's basically like a big brother
to me in the acting world.

190
00:10:10,548 --> 00:10:13,551
For an extra, you sure managed
to win over the guy playing Nobunaga.

191
00:10:13,634 --> 00:10:15,010
Stop saying extra over and over.

192
00:10:15,094 --> 00:10:17,471
Hey, is he staying here tonight?

193
00:10:17,555 --> 00:10:19,098
What are we doing for dinner?

194
00:10:19,181 --> 00:10:21,559
For now, just let him hide out here!

195
00:10:21,642 --> 00:10:23,477
Tokyo is crawling with reporters,
it's dangerous.

196
00:10:23,561 --> 00:10:28,023
Mr. Jin does a lot of commercials, right?
The cancellation penalties must be huge.

197
00:10:28,107 --> 00:10:30,484
Yeah, probably around a hundred
or two hundred million yen.

198
00:10:30,568 --> 00:10:32,027
What? That much?

199
00:10:33,654 --> 00:10:36,782
It feels great out here.

200
00:10:37,658 --> 00:10:41,328
Makes me want a beer.

201
00:10:41,412 --> 00:10:42,288
A beer?

202
00:10:42,371 --> 00:10:45,249
I'll get you one right now.

203
00:10:45,332 --> 00:10:46,834
Mr. Jin, here you go.

204
00:10:46,917 --> 00:10:48,669
-Thank you.
-No prob.

205
00:10:51,756 --> 00:10:55,676
I don't want to give up on health
or that refreshing feel!

206
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:58,429
For middle-aged people like you!

207
00:10:59,513 --> 00:11:00,473
This…

208
00:11:00,556 --> 00:11:02,892
This is the one I did a commercial for!

209
00:11:02,975 --> 00:11:04,018
I'm sorry.

210
00:11:04,602 --> 00:11:07,980
I'm sure the contract for
this commercial is getting terminated.

211
00:11:08,063 --> 00:11:11,650
And the penalties
are going to be astronomical.

212
00:11:11,734 --> 00:11:13,944
How about some tea instead?

213
00:11:16,655 --> 00:11:20,826
Burning middle-aged fat,
"Body Burning Tea."

214
00:11:20,910 --> 00:11:22,703
Now on sale!

215
00:11:22,786 --> 00:11:25,206
I did the commercial for this one too!

216
00:11:25,289 --> 00:11:26,415
Mr. Jin, calm down!

217
00:11:26,499 --> 00:11:30,878
Here, please,
take a seat in this chair, relax.

218
00:11:30,961 --> 00:11:33,088
I did an advertisement for this too.

219
00:11:33,172 --> 00:11:37,009
The brand ambassador for adult camping.

220
00:11:37,092 --> 00:11:37,968
What?

221
00:11:38,052 --> 00:11:41,472
Oh! Mr. Jin!
Please wipe your tears with these!

222
00:11:46,268 --> 00:11:50,981
Gently embracing your tears with softness.

223
00:11:51,607 --> 00:11:54,151
He really is incredible.
He has commercials for everything.

224
00:11:54,235 --> 00:11:57,279
-I did a commercial for this too.
-That's easily a billion yen right there.

225
00:11:57,363 --> 00:12:00,866
But honestly, I hear they don't usually
demand commercial penalties

226
00:12:00,950 --> 00:12:02,117
just for a suspected affair.

227
00:12:02,201 --> 00:12:04,620
-Really?
-Yes, it's not like he committed a crime.

228
00:12:04,703 --> 00:12:05,579
True.

229
00:12:05,663 --> 00:12:08,707
Still, things are going to be tough
for him as an actor from now on.

230
00:12:08,791 --> 00:12:11,585
That's true. He played many roles
with a strong sense of justice.

231
00:12:11,669 --> 00:12:15,047
Why would he even have an affair
when he has a wife?

232
00:12:15,130 --> 00:12:17,299
-What an absolute piece of garbage.
-Yeah.

233
00:12:17,383 --> 00:12:19,760
There's nowhere left
for him to go but hell.

234
00:12:19,843 --> 00:12:21,220
You guys are pretty harsh.

235
00:12:24,473 --> 00:12:26,141
Thank you for the firewood.

236
00:12:28,269 --> 00:12:29,812
Who is that gentleman?

237
00:12:29,895 --> 00:12:32,898
Oh, he's a famous actor.

238
00:12:32,982 --> 00:12:35,192
He appears in TV shows a lot.

239
00:12:35,276 --> 00:12:38,904
I used to watch
<i>From a Western Town in a Northern Country.</i>

240
00:12:39,697 --> 00:12:40,614
Listen up, Mr. Jin,

241
00:12:40,698 --> 00:12:44,118
I'm just going to say it,
but you brought this entirely on yourself!

242
00:12:44,201 --> 00:12:45,494
Hey, Midori.

243
00:12:45,578 --> 00:12:48,289
It's a hundred times harder on your wife.
She's crying more than you.

244
00:12:48,914 --> 00:12:50,457
And with three women on top of that.

245
00:12:50,541 --> 00:12:53,085
All those women
you cheated with are hurting too.

246
00:12:53,168 --> 00:12:55,337
That's right! You tell him, Midori!

247
00:12:55,421 --> 00:12:56,797
Stop it, Midori!

248
00:12:57,506 --> 00:12:58,799
No!

249
00:13:00,676 --> 00:13:02,303
I didn't do it.

250
00:13:04,513 --> 00:13:06,223
I even denied the affairs

251
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:10,352
through my agency.

252
00:13:11,895 --> 00:13:13,355
But the media

253
00:13:13,439 --> 00:13:17,484
just made up their minds
based on those photos.

254
00:13:19,153 --> 00:13:20,654
Do you have any idea?

255
00:13:22,031 --> 00:13:27,161
The <i>Weekly Shuubun</i> doesn't care
if they get sued for writing lies.

256
00:13:28,579 --> 00:13:29,622
Why?

257
00:13:30,205 --> 00:13:31,832
Because even if they lose,

258
00:13:31,915 --> 00:13:34,877
the damages are
a measly three million yen.

259
00:13:36,086 --> 00:13:37,463
So they write

260
00:13:38,839 --> 00:13:41,759
whatever lies sell magazines,
and that's all that matters to them.

261
00:13:44,261 --> 00:13:49,016
To people making
hundreds of millions off of fabrications,

262
00:13:50,392 --> 00:13:54,897
a lawsuit is nothing but a scratch.

263
00:13:56,774 --> 00:13:58,025
Meanwhile,

264
00:13:58,817 --> 00:14:02,404
because of that article,
they've stopped shooting my show.

265
00:14:03,697 --> 00:14:08,619
The movie wrap party
was targeted by reporters,

266
00:14:09,578 --> 00:14:15,751
and it has caused trouble
for my agency and other actors.

267
00:14:17,002 --> 00:14:18,879
This isn't anything new.

268
00:14:20,255 --> 00:14:22,299
But we celebrities

269
00:14:23,384 --> 00:14:27,930
are constantly getting screwed over
by their money-making schemes.

270
00:14:30,808 --> 00:14:33,978
Constantly screwed over.

271
00:14:35,688 --> 00:14:39,525
He really is so photogenic, so handsome!

272
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:44,113
Rinrin, you really don't have a specific
type when it comes to guys, do you?

273
00:14:44,196 --> 00:14:48,993
But, you know, I do feel a little bit
sorry for him looking at this.

274
00:14:49,076 --> 00:14:51,912
I WON'T WATCH HIS DRAMAS ANYMORE
HE'S OVER LOL

275
00:14:51,996 --> 00:14:53,622
WELL DONE SHUUBUN!

276
00:14:54,707 --> 00:14:56,792
I believe you, Mr. Jin.

277
00:14:57,459 --> 00:15:00,170
If it's for your sake,
I don't care if I get dragged too.

278
00:15:00,254 --> 00:15:02,131
Or if they write an article like,

279
00:15:02,214 --> 00:15:05,300
"Why is the rising star Konta
harboring a scumbag cheater actor?"

280
00:15:05,384 --> 00:15:06,677
Hey!

281
00:15:07,511 --> 00:15:10,889
We live in a terrible era.

282
00:15:11,682 --> 00:15:15,477
If it were just a magazine article,
only the people who read it would know.

283
00:15:15,561 --> 00:15:16,562
But now,

284
00:15:16,645 --> 00:15:21,650
follow-up articles keep popping up online,
and the fire keeps spreading.

285
00:15:21,734 --> 00:15:24,486
Hey, you're the number one
trending topic today.

286
00:15:24,570 --> 00:15:25,988
Damn it!

287
00:15:26,071 --> 00:15:29,616
Seriously, the <i>Weekly</i><i>Shuubun</i>
and the public. What are they doing?

288
00:15:30,451 --> 00:15:32,286
What's wrong with them?

289
00:15:32,953 --> 00:15:34,788
If you've got something to say,

290
00:15:35,581 --> 00:15:37,499
say it to my face!

291
00:15:37,583 --> 00:15:40,085
There it is! The classic Jin Ichijo style!

292
00:15:40,169 --> 00:15:41,462
Listen up.

293
00:15:42,046 --> 00:15:43,881
I didn't do it.

294
00:15:43,964 --> 00:15:45,966
I did not have an affair.

295
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:49,303
That article is a complete lie.

296
00:15:49,386 --> 00:15:53,057
Then what are those photos?

297
00:15:53,849 --> 00:15:55,017
Those are,

298
00:15:56,268 --> 00:15:57,603
in other words,

299
00:15:58,937 --> 00:16:00,481
a man and a woman.

300
00:16:05,861 --> 00:16:06,862
I can't hear you.

301
00:16:06,945 --> 00:16:09,823
But look, the photos are crystal clear.

302
00:16:09,907 --> 00:16:12,367
You can't really make excuses for this.

303
00:16:12,451 --> 00:16:15,079
In this one, you two
are embracing each other.

304
00:16:15,162 --> 00:16:17,498
If you didn't do it, is it photoshopped?

305
00:16:17,581 --> 00:16:19,124
Oh, AI?

306
00:16:19,875 --> 00:16:21,877
-Something smells good.
-What?

307
00:16:22,961 --> 00:16:24,880
The rainbow trout is ready.

308
00:16:24,963 --> 00:16:26,381
What? Already?

309
00:16:26,965 --> 00:16:28,550
I have to get the plates ready.

310
00:16:28,634 --> 00:16:29,718
Hey, wait…

311
00:16:29,802 --> 00:16:32,012
Yay, rainbow trout!

312
00:16:32,096 --> 00:16:34,848
Hold on a second.
I'm not finished talking.

313
00:16:34,932 --> 00:16:38,102
Hey! It's totally catching fire!
What do we do?

314
00:16:40,938 --> 00:16:42,356
-They're on fire!
-Oh, it's hot.

315
00:16:43,315 --> 00:16:44,525
I'm sorry.

316
00:16:44,608 --> 00:16:45,859
It seems like

317
00:16:45,943 --> 00:16:50,114
the fire over there requires a bit
more urgent attention than your fire.

318
00:16:50,197 --> 00:16:51,740
Are you okay?

319
00:16:54,201 --> 00:16:55,327
Yeah…

320
00:16:56,328 --> 00:17:00,165
Nobody ever actually listens
to what I have to say.

321
00:17:01,083 --> 00:17:03,085
I believe you, Mr. Jin.

322
00:17:03,168 --> 00:17:04,169
Midori!

323
00:17:04,253 --> 00:17:06,672
We siblings are going to support Mr. Jin!

324
00:17:06,755 --> 00:17:08,841
Wait, support?

325
00:17:10,759 --> 00:17:12,136
Your sister…

326
00:17:12,761 --> 00:17:14,054
Midori, was it?

327
00:17:14,638 --> 00:17:16,098
Oh, yes.

328
00:17:16,932 --> 00:17:20,769
I'm sorry for completely ruining
your vacation.

329
00:17:22,896 --> 00:17:24,189
But, please…

330
00:17:25,149 --> 00:17:26,900
Believe me.

331
00:17:41,456 --> 00:17:43,959
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

332
00:17:44,042 --> 00:17:47,588
You haven't happened to see
Jin Ichijo around here, have you?

333
00:17:49,965 --> 00:17:52,009
-Jin Ichijo?
-Yes.

334
00:17:52,801 --> 00:17:54,720
Oh, I am…

335
00:17:59,516 --> 00:18:01,101
with this publication.

336
00:18:01,185 --> 00:18:02,811
HARUFUMI MASUDA
WEEKLY SHUUBUN

337
00:18:32,633 --> 00:18:34,426
<i>A vacation, huh.</i>

338
00:18:34,509 --> 00:18:35,469
<i>Jin Ichijo.</i>

339
00:18:35,552 --> 00:18:37,971
<i>Surrounded by young girls</i>
<i>on a harem vacation</i>

340
00:18:38,055 --> 00:18:39,514
<i>in the middle of a major scandal…</i>

341
00:18:39,598 --> 00:18:40,432
What a scoop.

342
00:18:40,515 --> 00:18:42,226
Just how angry is your wife?

343
00:18:42,309 --> 00:18:43,393
<i>Are you getting a divorce?</i>

344
00:18:43,477 --> 00:18:44,645
Who might you be?

345
00:18:44,728 --> 00:18:47,481
<i>My apologies for showing up unannounced.</i>

346
00:18:47,564 --> 00:18:50,817
Konta's special summer
orange sour drink is ready!

347
00:18:50,901 --> 00:18:52,277
Grovel!

348
00:18:52,819 --> 00:18:54,071
Grovel!

349
00:18:54,571 --> 00:18:57,574
Vacations are the best!

350
00:18:58,075 --> 00:18:59,117
Are you leaving already?

351
00:19:00,369 --> 00:19:02,955
You don't look like an ordinary person.

352
00:19:03,038 --> 00:19:04,414
<i>I don't look…</i>

353
00:19:05,499 --> 00:19:07,209
like a normal person?

354
00:19:07,709 --> 00:19:08,669
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.

